    {
      "id": "r20261107-a02",
      "title": "The App That Reads to the Blind",
      "level": "Menengah",
      "min": 3,
      "body": [
        "For many blind people, reading a restaurant menu or a street sign is impossible without help. A free smartphone app is changing that. With one tap, it connects a blind user to a sighted volunteer anywhere in the world.",
        "The volunteer sees the user’s camera and reads whatever is in front of it: the expiry date on a milk carton, the number of an arriving bus, or a letter from the bank. Calls usually last less than two minutes, but they make a big difference.",
        "There are now over six million volunteers and only about five hundred thousand blind users, so help almost always comes within seconds. \"I feel independent again,\" says Rini, a user from Bandung. \"I don’t have to wait for my family to read things for me.\""
      ],
      "gloss": {
        "blind": "tunanetra",
        "sign": "rambu/papan",
        "tap": "ketukan layar",
        "sighted": "dapat melihat",
        "volunteer": "relawan",
        "expiry date": "tanggal kedaluwarsa",
        "difference": "dampak besar",
        "independent": "mandiri"
      },
      "qs": [
